1174 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H1
/P 376 0 R
/T (However, smartphones are also incredibly powerful tools that can actually enhance learning. Many educational apps, online research tools, and even digital textbooks are accessible via smartphones. For instance, a student could use their phone to quickly look up an unfamiliar word, access a relevant historical document for a project, or even use a language learning app during breaks. Banning them entirely removes these educational opportunities.)
/E (However, smartphones are also incredibly powerful tools that can actually enhance learning. Many educational apps, online research tools, and even digital textbooks are accessible via smartphones. For instance, a student could use their phone to quickly look up an unfamiliar word, access a relevant historical document for a project, or even use a language learning app during breaks. Banning them entirely removes these educational opportunities.)
/Pg 71 0 R
/K [4]
>>
endobj
1175 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H1
/P 376 0 R
/T (Therefore, instead of an outright ban, I believe schools should focus on teaching responsible digital citizenship and integrating smartphones as learning aids. Setting clear rules, like phones being put away during direct instruction but allowed for specific research tasks, could be a good compromise.)
