/T (On one hand, subjects like math and science are fundamental. They build critical thinking, problem-solving abilities, and provide the foundational knowledge for many careers. Understanding physics or algebra isn't just about passing tests; it's about developing a logical mindset that's useful in many aspects of life. For instance, a grasp of scientific principles helps us understand the world around us, from weather patterns to how our bodies work.)
